+# Attack log: `parseCsvLine` (round 1)
+
+Target: `parseCsvLine` in `src/csv.mjs`, judged solely against the contract in
+`README.md`. Method: read the README clause by clause, read the scanner, then
+run probes from the project root with `node` (scratch scripts were kept under
+`traces/_scratch/` while running and deleted afterwards; `traces/` holds only
+failing traces, of which this round produced none).
+
+Baseline: `npm test` passes 37/37.
+
+## Surfaces attacked
+
+### 1. Differential check against an independent oracle
+
+Wrote a second parser directly from the README as a recursive-descent grammar
+(structured differently from both `src/csv.mjs` and the state-machine oracle in
+`tests/csv.test.mjs`), then compared outcomes (fields vs. CsvError) and checked
+that every return value is a plain `Array` of primitive strings and every throw
+is a `CsvError` that is also an `Error`.
+
+- Exhaustive: every string up to length 8 over `" , \n \r a` (488,281 strings).
+- Exhaustive: every string up to length 7 over `" , \n \r a space tab` (960,800).
+- Random: 500,000 strings up to 60 chars over a 26-symbol alphabet that adds
+  `\r\n`, `\0`, NEL (U+0085), U+2028, U+2029, BOM (U+FEFF), ideographic space
+  (U+3000), an emoji, lone high and low surrogates, `é`, `\`, `'`, fullwidth
+  comma (U+FF0C) and curly quotes (U+201C/D).
+
+Result: 0 mismatches, no non-CsvError throws, no non-array / non-string results.
+
+### 2. Clause-by-clause hand-picked cases (about 120)
+
+- Separators / empty fields: `""`, `a,`, `,a`, `,,`, `"",,`, `,,""`, mixtures of
+  quoted and unquoted empties.
+- Quoting: `""""`, `"""`, `"""""`, `""""""`, `""a`, `"""a"`, `"a""`, `"a"""`,
+  `"a""""`, `"x""y""z"`, `"x"",""y"`, backslash before a quote (`"a\"` parses,
+  `"a\""` is unterminated), single/curly quotes literal.
+- After closing quote: letter, space, tab, `\r`, BOM, NBSP, emoji, NEL, second
+  terminator, `\n,` all rejected; `,`, `\n`, `\r\n`, end accepted.
+- Outside-quote `"`: ` "a"`, `a "b"`, `a,"b"c`, `a,"b" ,c`, `﻿"a"`,
+  `\ud800"` all CsvError.
+- Whitespace: leading/trailing spaces, tabs, `\v`, `\f`, U+3000 kept verbatim.
+- Terminators: every combination of `\n`, `\r`, `\r\n` at start, middle and end,
+  doubled (`\n\n`, `\r\n\r\n`, `\n\r`, `\r\r\n`, `\r\n\n`, `\n\r\n`), lone
+  trailing `\r`, terminator directly after a quoted field, quoted `\r`, `\r\n`,
+  `\n` inside quotes with and without a trailing terminator, a `\n` "closing"
+  an open quote (`"a\n`, `"\n`, `"a""\n`, `a,"\n`, `",\n`).
+- Literal characters: `\0`, ESC, U+0085, U+2028/2029, BOM at start / inside
+  quotes / after a closing quote, lone surrogates in every position, emoji,
+  CJK, fullwidth comma, semicolon, backslash-comma.
+
+All results agreed with the README.
+
+### 3. Non-string input and calling conventions
+
+`undefined`, `null`, numbers, `NaN`, booleans, `{}`, `[]`, `["a"]`,
+`new String("a,b")` (same realm and from a `vm` context), `Symbol`, `BigInt`,
+functions, `Buffer`, `Date`, `RegExp`, `Proxy` around a String object,
+null-prototype objects, objects with `Symbol.toPrimitive` / `valueOf`, Promise,
+Map, `Uint16Array`, `ArrayBuffer`, `Error`, `Boolean`/`Number` objects, and a
+duck-typed object exposing `length`/`charCodeAt`/`indexOf`/`slice`: every one
+throws a bare `TypeError` (not a `CsvError`). No arguments throws `TypeError`.
+Extra arguments, `call(null, ...)`, `new parseCsvLine(...)` and a cross-realm
+string primitive all parse normally.
+
+### 4. Result shape, mutation and state leakage
+
+- Each call returns a fresh array (`a !== b`), prototype `Array.prototype`,
+  own keys only `0..n-1` and `length`, every element `typeof "string"`.
+- Mutating a returned array (push, overwrite) does not affect later calls.
+- A `CsvError` on one call does not affect the next call.
+- `Object.prototype` and `Array.prototype` pollution does not leak into results.
+- `CsvError`: `name === "CsvError"`, `instanceof Error`, `String(e)` sane,
+  `new CsvError()` with no args does not throw; extra `index` property is
+  outside the contract and harmless.
+
+### 5. Performance / hang probes
+
+25 shapes, each at 100 KB, 1 MB and 10 MB, timed with `process.hrtime`
+(first call cold, no warm-up):
+
+one huge unquoted field; only commas; one huge quoted field; all quotes (even
+and odd count); `"` followed by 50k `""` pairs (unterminated); `"",` repeated;
+`"""",` repeated; `"a""b",` repeated; emoji + escaped quote fields (two-byte
+string representation); two-byte unquoted fields; `"` error at the very last
+byte; `\r` at the very last byte; quoted field with garbage at the last byte;
+`"\r\n",` repeated; `\n` at index 0 of a huge input; a cons-string built by
+repeated `+=`; a sliced-string view; 1-char fields; quoted 1-char fields;
+huge quoted field followed by a stray `"`; escaped quote every 2nd character;
+runs of 8 escaped quotes; huge quoted field with trailing `\r\n`; 100 KB of
+lone surrogates.
+
+Worst observed: 100 KB 4.1 ms, 1 MB 25 ms, 10 MB 207 ms (only-commas,
+10.5 M fields). Time scales linearly; nothing approaches the 1 s budget and
+nothing hangs.
+
+## Outcome
+
+No behaviour contradicting any README clause was reproduced. No trace written.
+
+verdict: pass
