+# Changes
+
+## Round 0
+
+No traces yet; initial hardening of `parseCsvLine` against every clause of the
+contract in README.md.
+
+### src/csv.mjs
+
+Rewrote the parser as a single-pass, index-based scanner (the previous version
+was O(n^2) via `rest.slice(1)` and enforced almost none of the contract).
+
+Hardened:
+
+- Non-string input (including `String` objects, Buffers, arrays, objects with
+  `toString`, symbols, bigints, `undefined`) throws `TypeError`, never
+  `CsvError`.
+- Empty text is `[""]`; leading, trailing and consecutive commas produce empty
+  fields.
+- Quoted fields: `""` inside quotes is one `"`; commas, `\n`, `\r\n`, lone
+  `\r`, tabs, control characters and any Unicode inside quotes are literal.
+- After a closing quote only `,`, the record terminator or end of text may
+  follow; anything else (space, tab, letter, `\r`, a second terminator,
+  NBSP, BOM, emoji, U+2028/2029, NEL) is a `CsvError`.
+- An unterminated quoted field is a `CsvError` (including odd runs of quotes
+  and quotes "closed" only by the trailing terminator).
+- A `"` anywhere outside quotes is a `CsvError` (`a"b`, `a "b"`, `a"`, ` "a"`,
+  `a,"b"c`, ...). A quote only opens a field at the field's first character.
+- Whitespace outside quotes (space, tab, NBSP, ideographic space, `\f`, `\v`)
+  is kept as part of the field.
+- Exactly one `\n` or `\r\n` at the very end is stripped; any other unquoted
+  `\r` or `\n` (lone trailing `\r`, `\r\r\n`, `\n\n`, `\n\r`, mid-record
+  breaks, leading breaks) is a `CsvError`.
+- Every other character is literal: `\0`, ESC, `\u0085`, BOM, U+2028/2029,
+  lone surrogates, fullwidth comma, curly quotes, backslash (not an escape).
+- Linear time and no recursion: 100 KB records of every shape (one huge field,
+  50k fields, only commas, only escaped quotes, errors at the very end) parse
+  or fail in a few milliseconds; a 1 MB record in ~20 ms.
+- Only `string[]` or `CsvError` ever leave the function for string input.
+  `CsvError` carries an `index` (offset of the fault).
+
+### tests/csv.test.mjs
+
+Extended from 4 tests to 37: one or more tests per README clause (listed
+above), README examples, exhaustive TypeError cases, result-shape and
+statelessness properties, 12 performance tests at 100 KB / 1 MB with a
+1-second budget, a seeded 20,000-case differential fuzz against an
+independent state-machine oracle, an exhaustive check of every string up to
+length 6 over the alphabet `" , \n \r a space` (55,987 strings), and a
+5,000-case encode/parse round-trip property.
